.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt DEVCTL 4
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devctl
.Nd device event device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/devctl
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The kernel reports each change to the system's devices as an event: a disk
attached or detached, a
.Pa /dev
node made or removed, a CD's disc found or gone, the root's drive lost.
Each event is one line of text,
.Pp
.Dl Ar verb class Op Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Pp
ended by a newline.
Verbs, classes and field names are lower-case words.
A value of only letters, digits and
.Ql _./:+-,@%
is written bare; any other is written in single quotes, as
.Xr sh 1
quotes it, with an embedded single quote written as
.Ql \(aq\e\(aq\(aq .
A control character in a value is written
.Ql \&? ,
so a device's own strings, such as a drive's model name, can neither end a
line nor add fields to it.
.Pp
The events are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li attach disk Va name bus model kind sectors sector_size
A disk or CD drive was found, at boot or plugged in.
.Va bus
is
.Li ahci ,
.Li ata ,
.Li virtio_blk ,
.Li virtio_scsi
or
.Li md ;
.Va kind
is
.Li disk
or
.Li cd ;
.Va sectors
counts 512-byte sectors (0 for an empty CD drive) and
.Va sector_size
is the drive's own.
An AHCI drive also has
.Va controller
and
.Va port ,
and
.Va pmp
behind a port multiplier.
.It Li detach disk Va name bus
A drive was pulled out, after its file systems were unmounted.
.It Li create dev Va name major minor
A
.Pa /dev
node was made;
.Va name
is relative to
.Pa /dev .
.It Li destroy dev Va name major minor
A
.Pa /dev
node was removed.
.It Li media cd Va name Li state=inserted Va sectors
A disc was found in CD drive
.Va name .
.It Li media cd Va name Li state=ejected
CD drive
.Va name Ns 's
disc is gone.
.It Li lost root Va name Li policy=eio
The root file system's drive went, and the system keeps running
.Po
.Va kern.disk.root_lost
is
.Li eio
.Pc .
.It Li lost devctl Va count
.Va count
events were dropped before this one.
.El
.Pp
When a drive is attached its
.Li attach disk
line comes first, then the whole disk's
.Li create dev ,
then, for a CD drive with a disc,
.Li media cd state=inserted ,
then each partition's
.Li create dev .
When it is detached the
.Li destroy dev
lines come first, then
.Li detach disk .
A reader ignores verbs, classes and fields it does not know: more come with
new drivers.
.Pp
The kernel queues events from boot, whether or not the device is open, so a
reader sees the drives found at boot as if they had just been plugged in.
The queue holds
.Va kern.devctl.queue
lines (256 by default, at least 16); when it is full the oldest is dropped and
counted in
.Va kern.devctl.dropped ,
and the next line read is
.Li lost devctl count= Ns Ar n .
.Pp
The character device
.Pa /dev/devctl ,
number 7, 1, owned by root with mode 0600, reads the queue, normally for
.Xr devd 8 .
Only one descriptor may have it open at a time, and only for reading.
A
.Xr read 2
takes as many bytes off the queue as fit, a line that does not fit given in
part and finished by the next read; closing the device drops the rest of
such a line, so the next reader starts on a whole one.
With the queue empty a read waits for an event, or fails with
.Er EAGAIN
if the descriptor is non-blocking; a signal interrupts the wait.
.Xr poll 2
reports the descriptor readable while the queue holds anything.
Events that come while nobody has the device open wait in the queue.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/devctl -compact
.It Pa /dev/devctl
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A drive plugged into the third port of the first AHCI controller:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
attach disk name=sata0.2 bus=ahci model='WDC WD10EZEX-08W' kind=disk sectors=1953525168 sector_size=512 controller=0 port=2
create dev name=sata0.2 major=251 minor=512
create dev name=sata0.2p1 major=251 minor=513
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBUSY
.Xr open 2 :
another descriptor has the device open.
.It Bq Er EACCES
.Xr open 2 :
the device was opened for writing.
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
.Xr read 2 :
no event is queued and the descriptor is non-blocking.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devfs 4 ,
.Xr devd.conf 5 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Pa /dev/devctl
device first appeared in
.Fx 5.0 .
OxideBSD's events are its own: shell-quoted
.Ar verb class name Ns = Ns Ar value
lines instead of FreeBSD's
.Ql !system=
and
.Ql +device
forms.
